---
import { Code } from 'astro:components';

const workerExample = `import { OpfsVfs, OpenFlags } from '@opfs-vfs/opfs-vfs';

const fs = new OpfsVfs('project.bin');
await fs.ready;

const content: Uint8Array = new TextEncoder().encode('Hello');
const fd = fs.openSync('/notes.txt',
  OpenFlags.O_CREAT | OpenFlags.O_RDWR);
try {
  fs.writeSync(fd, content);
  fs.fsyncSync(fd);
} finally {
  fs.closeSync(fd);
}
await fs.closeVfs();`;
---
<section class="inspectable" id="inspectable-files" aria-labelledby="inspectable-heading">
  <header class="benefit-heading">
    <div><p class="kicker">See what you store</p><h2 id="inspectable-heading">Find the file.<br />Read what it holds.</h2></div>
    <div class="benefit-intro"><p>Browse the file behind a bug, inspect its contents, and edit it in place. Volume Explorer and the just-bash shell work directly with your OPFS VFS files.</p><a class="text-link" href="/demos/filesystem/">Explore a real volume <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
  </header>
  <div class="storage-comparison">
    <figure class="record-view">
      <figcaption><span class="example-label">An app-specific IndexedDB layout</span><strong>What do these entries contain?</strong></figcaption>
      <dl class="records">
        <div><dt>chunk:8f2a:0</dt><dd>ArrayBuffer(4096)</dd></div>
        <div><dt>chunk:8f2a:1</dt><dd>ArrayBuffer(1024)</dd></div>
        <div><dt>inode:8f2a</dt><dd>&#123; blocks: [0, 1], … &#125;</dd></div>
      </dl>
      <p>DevTools shows the records. Making sense of the files may mean decoding the application's keys, chunks, and metadata.</p>
      <span class="illustration-note">Illustrative records. Filesystem layouts vary.</span>
    </figure>
    <figure class="file-view">
      <figcaption><span class="example-label">With OPFS VFS tools</span><strong>A path to the file you need.</strong></figcaption>
      <pre class="file-tree" aria-label="Example workspace file tree"><code>/workspace
├── documents/
│   └── <span class="file-name">notes.md</span>
└── data/
    └── <span class="file-name">results.csv</span></code></pre>
      <div class="shell-example"><span class="example-label">Read it with just-bash</span><pre><code><span aria-hidden="true">$ </span>cat /workspace/documents/notes.md
<span class="file-content">Ideas for the next release.</span></code></pre></div>
      <span class="illustration-note">Example paths and file contents.</span>
    </figure>
  </div>
  <p class="comparison-note">IndexedDB can also power a filesystem and explorer. OPFS VFS brings the path API, explorer, previews, and just-bash integration together. Files live inside a browser-local volume, not in folders on your desktop.</p>
</section>
<section class="sync-benefit" id="synchronous-io" aria-labelledby="sync-heading">
  <div class="sync-copy">
    <p class="kicker">Synchronous at the core</p>
    <h2 id="sync-heading">File I/O.<br />Without the<br /><span>await.</span></h2>
    <p>After setup, reads and writes return directly inside a dedicated worker. No promise round trip for each file operation.</p>
    <p>Useful for databases, WebAssembly runtimes, and workloads with many small operations. Your interface stays connected through the asynchronous worker client.</p>
    <a class="text-link" href="/benchmarks/run/">Compare real workloads <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
  </div>
  <figure class="worker-example">
    <figcaption><span>worker.ts</span><span>TypeScript · Dedicated worker</span></figcaption>
    <Code code={workerExample} lang="ts" theme="css-variables" tabindex="0" aria-label="TypeScript filesystem example" />
    <p>Await setup once. Read and write synchronously.<br />Synchronize important writes before closing the file.</p>
  </figure>
  <p class="sync-note">IndexedDB uses asynchronous requests. Actual throughput depends on the workload, browser, buffering, and durability settings. <a href="/benchmarks/storage/">Compare storage settings.</a></p>
  <div class="durability-note"><span class="kicker">Persistence you control</span><p>Disk buffering and balanced durability are the defaults. Choose when to synchronize important writes, then reopen the same volume in your next session.</p><a class="text-link" href="/docs/guides/persistence/">How saving works <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
</section>
<style>
  section { scroll-margin-top: 32px; }
  .inspectable { padding: clamp(48px, 7vw, 96px) 0 64px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .benefit-heading { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.4fr 1fr; align-items: end; gap: 64px; margin-bottom: 64px; }
  .kicker { margin: 0 0 20px; }
  h2 { font-size: clamp(38px, 5vw, 68px); line-height: 1.02; margin: 0; }
  .benefit-intro p, .sync-copy > p:not(.kicker) { color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.7; font-size: 16px; max-width: 440px; margin: 0 0 18px; }
  .storage-comparison { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.4fr; gap: 64px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding-top: 32px; }
  figure { min-width: 0; margin: 0; }
  .record-view { padding-top: 8px; }
  .file-view { border-left: 1px solid var(--line); padding-left: clamp(24px, 5vw, 64px); }
  .example-label { display: block; color: var(--muted); font: 11px/1.5 ui-monospace, monospace; }
  figcaption strong { display: block; margin-top: 12px; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: -.025em; }
  .records { margin: 32px 0; font: 12px/1.7 ui-monospace, monospace; color: var(--muted); }
  .records > div { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 4px 14px; padding: 12px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .records dd { margin: 0; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .record-view p { color: var(--muted); font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.65; max-width: 350px; }
  .illustration-note { display: block; color: var(--muted); font-size: 11px; line-height: 1.5; margin-top: 20px; }
  pre { overflow-x: auto; font: 13px/1.85 ui-monospace, monospace; }
  code { font: inherit; }
  .file-tree { color: var(--accent); font-size: clamp(17px, 2vw, 26px); line-height: 1.7; margin: 30px 0; }
  .file-name { color: var(--ink); }
  .shell-example { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding-top: 20px; }
  .shell-example pre { margin: 10px 0 0; color: var(--accent); font-size: 12px; }
  .file-content { color: var(--muted); }
  .comparison-note { max-width: 720px; color: var(--muted); font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.7; margin: 36px 0 0; }
  .sync-benefit { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.4fr; gap: 36px 64px; align-items: start; padding: 64px 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .sync-copy h2 { margin-bottom: 28px; }
  .sync-copy h2 span { color: var(--accent); font-family: ui-monospace, monospace; font-weight: 400; }
  .text-link { display: inline-block; color: var(--accent); font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; text-underline-offset: 5px; padding: 8px 0; }
  .worker-example {
    padding-top: 2px;
    --astro-code-color-text: var(--ink);
    --astro-code-color-background: transparent;
    --astro-code-token-constant: var(--accent);
    --astro-code-token-string: var(--accent);
    --astro-code-token-keyword: var(--accent);
    --astro-code-token-function: var(--ink);
    --astro-code-token-parameter: var(--ink);
    --astro-code-token-punctuation: var(--muted);
    --astro-code-token-comment: var(--muted);
    --astro-code-token-string-expression: var(--accent);
  }
  .worker-example figcaption { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; padding: 0 0 18px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); color: var(--muted); font: 11px/1.5 ui-monospace, monospace; }
  .worker-example figcaption > span:first-child { color: var(--ink); }
  .worker-example :global(pre) { margin: 0; padding: 26px 0; background: transparent !important; font: 12px/1.85 ui-monospace, monospace; }
  .worker-example :global(code) { font: inherit; }
  .worker-example p { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding-top: 18px; color: var(--muted); font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.7; margin: 0; }
  .sync-note { grid-column: 2; font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--muted); margin: 0; max-width: 550px; }
  .sync-note a { text-underline-offset: 3px; }
  .durability-note { grid-column: 1 / -1; display: grid; grid-template-columns: auto 1fr auto; gap: 24px; align-items: center; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding-top: 24px; }
  .durability-note .kicker { margin: 0; }
  .durability-note p { margin: 0; max-width: 650px; color: var(--muted); font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.7; }
  a:focus-visible, .worker-example :global(pre:focus-visible) { outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 4px; }
  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .benefit-heading, .storage-comparison, .sync-benefit { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 32px; }
    .benefit-heading { margin-bottom: 40px; }
    .file-view { border-left: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 28px 0 0; }
    .sync-benefit { padding-top: 48px; }
    .sync-note { grid-column: 1; }
    .durability-note { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 10px; }
  }
</style>
